unpack # it by saving it into a file and typing "sh file".  To
overwrite existing # files, type "sh file -c".  You can also feed
this as standard input via # unshar, or by typing "sh <file", e.g.. 
If this archive is complete, you # will see the following message at
the end: #               "End of archive 1 (of 2)."
